v0.13: coverage reporting works in isolated mode too

- worker appends one coverage line per batch (S<TAB>id,id,...); the parent
  merges it into its own id set
- cov: merge_seen / encode_ids / decode_ids
- absorb and probe both recognise the coverage line (probe only merges, it never
  counts as a candidate result)
- two bugs fixed on the way: the worker never called commit(), and the fold loop
  stopped at batch.length() and silently dropped the trailing line
- 104 tests native / 85 wasm-gc